Here's an example code snippet that demonstrates how to intercept an event and allow propagation:
```javascript
// Get a reference to the element you want to listen for events on
const myElement = document.getElementById('my-element');

// Add an event listener for the 'click' event
myElement.addEventListener('click', function(event) {
  // Intercept the event and perform some action
  console.log('Click event intercepted!');

